From d0a9b6cab26f3adeac32f02f19c99ba8543e906d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:52:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: the HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame built on zeroes, with
 3D_Meta_present in bit 3

NvTiming_ConstructVendorSpecificInfoframe() sets the frame one field at a
time with nvt_nvu8_set_bits() and did not clear it first, so a bit that no
branch writes kept whatever the caller's memory held. NVKMS's own caller,
SendVendorSpecificInfoFrame(), builds the frame on its stack:

- frame packing, the 3D mode that NVKMS signals itself
  (ConstructVSInfoFrameCtrl()): bit 3 of PB5, 3D_Meta_present, was never
  written. On a host build of the NVKMS code with NVIDIA's packet library
  it went out as 1 (PB5 0x08) in some frame packing scenarios and as 0 in
  others; with -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero always as 0, with =pattern
  always as 1. A display that honours the bit reads the byte after PB5 as
  the header of 3D metadata;
- side-by-side half: the low nibble of PB6, reserved;
- the HF-VSIF: the bits of PB5 other than ALLM (NVKMS does not send it).

The frame is now cleared after the parameter check, as
NvTiming_ConstructExtendedMetadataPacketInfoframe() does. A client's
vendor InfoFrame (NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA, the one of Dolby Vision) does not
go through this function and does not change.

NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_3D_META_PRESENT_MASK was 0x01 with a shift of 3, but
nvt_nvu8_set_bits() and nvt_get_bits() take the mask already shifted, as
every other mask of the library is written: "not present" cleared bit 0
(reserved, and cleared already) instead of bit 3, and "present" set
nothing. It is 0x08 now. Of the 86 calls of those macros in the tree, the
four with this mask, all in this function, are the only ones whose mask
and shift do not agree. NVKMS never asks for metadata (MetadataPresent is
0), so the mask changes no byte that NVKMS sends: the host build sends
the same bytes with the frame cleared and either mask. The rest of the
metadata path is left as it is, and is not reached: its copy goes from
the frame into the control, and its type and length byte is not laid out
as in HDMI 1.4b.

Measured on the host: every harness of NVKMS gives the same bytes with no
init of the stack, =zero and =pattern, and the bytes that a zeroed stack
gave before; with the LG C5, which does not declare HDMI 3D, nothing
changes.
---
 src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c | 9 +++++++++
 src/common/modeset/timing/nvtiming.h        | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c b/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c
index fa63f98..3a4b302 100644
--- a/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c
+++ b/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c
@@ -2867,6 +2867,15 @@ NVT_STATUS NvTiming_ConstructVendorSpecificInfoframe(NVT_EDID_INFO *pEdidInfo, N
         return NVT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
     }
 
+    //
+    // Hades: the frame is built on zeroes, as NvTiming_ConstructExtendedMetadataPacketInfoframe()
+    // does. The fields below are set one by one with nvt_nvu8_set_bits(), and a bit that no case
+    // writes went out as whatever the caller's memory held: bit 3 of PB5 (3D_Meta_present) in
+    // the frame packing InfoFrame that NVKMS sends from its stack, the low nibble of PB6 for
+    // side-by-side half, and the bits of the HF-VSIF PB5 other than ALLM.
+    //
+    NVMISC_MEMSET(pInfoFrame, 0, sizeof(*pInfoFrame));
+
     // infoframe is only supported on 861A and later
     if (pEdidInfo->ext861.revision < NVT_CEA861_REV_A)
     {
diff --git a/src/common/modeset/timing/nvtiming.h b/src/common/modeset/timing/nvtiming.h
index 4a6ac69..eee55eb 100644
--- a/src/common/modeset/timing/nvtiming.h
+++ b/src/common/modeset/timing/nvtiming.h
@@ -3833,7 +3833,7 @@ typedef struct tagNVT_VENDOR_SPECIFIC_INFOFRAME
 //
 #define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_HDMI_RSVD_MASK            0x07    // HDMI_VID_FMT = HDMI_VID_FMT_3D
 #define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_HDMI_RSVD_SHIFT           0x00
-#define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_3D_META_PRESENT_MASK      0x01
+#define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_3D_META_PRESENT_MASK      0x08    // Hades: bit 3, shifted as nvt_nvu8_set_bits() takes every mask (was 0x01)
 #define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_3D_META_PRESENT_SHIFT     0x03
 #define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_HDMI_META_PRESENT_NOTPRES 0x00    // HDMI Metadata is not present
 #define NVT_HDMI_VS_BYTE5_HDMI_META_PRESENT_PRES    0x01    // HDMI Metadata is present
-- 
2.53.0

